course: dictionary
lesson: 11987
title: Cession: giving land away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cession is the act of giving up land or rights to another country or person. It often happens after a war, when one side hands land over to the other.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «After the war, the cession of the land was agreed in a treaty.» A treaty is a formal written agreement, and land was handed over to someone else, so cession must mean giving land away.
explain: Cession is a formal word, so you will meet it mostly in history and law. In everyday talk, people say "handing over" or "giving up" instead.
fact: Cession means the act of giving up land or rights to another country or person.
fact: «The Mexican Cession» of 1848 was land that Mexico handed over to the United States.
fact: «Hong Kong's cession to Britain» means Hong Kong was handed over to Britain.
fact: Cessions often happen after a war or by a treaty, which is a formal written agreement.
fact: Phrases to know: «the cession of» (followed by the land given up) and «land cession».
exercise: «The treaty approved the cession of the land to the other country.» What does cession mean here? | A soldier's rank | *The giving up of land to another country | A map showing hills and rivers | A big party to celebrate the end of a war
exercise: «After the war, the cession of the land was agreed in a treaty.» What does cession mean here? | A big party to celebrate the end of the war | A soldier's rank | *Handing land over to another country | A map showing hills and rivers
exercise: «The two countries signed a treaty for the cession of the island.» Find and copy the word that means a formal written agreement. | cession | countries | island | *treaty
test: «Hong Kong's cession to Britain changed who ruled the island.» Cession here means: | Painting a picture of the island | Visiting the island on holiday | *Handing the island over to Britain | Building a new bridge to the island
test: Which sentence uses cession correctly? | The cession was a bright blue colour | *The war ended with a cession of land to the winning side | He made a cession of his bike to the dog | She had a cession of pizza for lunch
exam: «Mexico made a cession of land after the war in 1848.» What does this mean? | Mexico held a big party | *Mexico gave up land to another country | Mexico built a new road | Mexico bought a new car
